\chapter{Test Patterns}\label{ch:patterns}

Natural photographs make poor test inputs for a resampler. Their spectrum is unknown, so it's hard
to tell whether a ripple in a profile comes from the image or from the filter. Synthetic patterns
have known spectra, and each one stresses one property: a chirp sweeps all frequencies, an edge
shows ringing, an impulse shows the point-spread function. LineScope can generate eleven such
patterns. The generator lives in the core package, so the tests can use it too.

